*_ss.csv
# ...except this one.  m6_calibration.py and extract_pls.py both read it, so
# a clean checkout that does not have it reports a DIFFERENT number of checks
# than the workstation does -- and a check count that depends on the machine
# is not a check.  It is a verification input, not an analysis leftover.
!data/properties/M5_c26k_T1000_ss.csv
# ...and the M6 curves, for exactly the same reason.  check_ch4_numbers 4.9-0a
# (a2, R4-A-3) opens LTH_M6_*_ss.csv and re-derives the peaks and tangents from
# them.  On the workstation those files exist untracked, so the gate is green
# there and red on every clean checkout -- the same failure mode refs/[73] had.
# Un-ignoring them here does not commit them; a2 still has to add the files.
!data/results/M6/*_ss.csv
ss_curves_by_temperature.png
dist/*.pdf
